{"document":3,"title":"user in #e9327a54:c58fdf1e_2: I'm trying to plan my meals for the next week and...","updated_at":"2023-05-21T06:38:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"I'm trying to plan my meals for the next week and I was wondering if you could suggest some recipes that use chicken breast. I've been buying it in bulk lately and I want to use it up before it expires. By the way, I've been trying to reduce my grocery spending, and I'm glad I stocked up on some staples last week at Walmart - it really helped. Speaking of which, I had a fun trip to Trader Joe's the week before that with my sister and we spent around $80 between the two of us.","metadata":"{"Channel": "e9327a54:c58fdf1e_2"}"}
{"document":4,"title":"user in #e9327a54:61e1ba53_2: I'm looking for some brunch recommendations in the...","updated_at":"2023-05-24T10:26:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"assistant:You're welcome! I'm glad I could help.

According to my knowledge, The Egg & I is a first-come, first-served restaurant, so I'd recommend arriving early to snag a table, especially on weekends. As for the service, they're generally pretty quick, but it can vary depending on the crowd. If you're planning to spend a few hours there, you might want to consider getting there a bit earlier to grab a table and then take your time enjoying your meal. They do have a pretty extensive menu, so you might want to factor in some extra time to decide!

Also, since you mentioned trying out new brunch spots, I'm curious - what did you like about the new place you tried downtown last week? Was there a particular dish or atmosphere that stood out to you?

I think I'll get there around 10 am to beat the crowd. And yeah, their menu does look pretty extensive, so we'll probably take our time deciding.

As for the new place I tried last week, I think what really stood out to me was the unique dishes they had. They had a lot of creative twists on classic brunch items, which was really refreshing. And the atmosphere was really trendy and modern, which was a nice change of pace from the usual breakfast joints. But what really impressed me was the service - our server was super friendly and attentive, and the food came out really quickly. Overall, it was just a really great experience!","metadata":"{"Channel": "e9327a54:61e1ba53_2"}"}
